  "verbalization": "Pandaroside I is implicated in the interaction with A549 cells through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in cellular processes that may contribute to its biological activity. The evidence suggests that Pandaroside I acts as a target for multiple compounds, including MIP and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn target A549 cells. These targets are likely involved in pathways that influence cell behavior, potentially through mechanisms such as receptor activation or signaling cascades. The presence of multiple targets, each with a clear link to A549, indicates a potential role for Pandaroside I in modulating cellular functions relevant to A549 cell viability or proliferation. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction, with the exact mechanism of action remaining to be fully elucidated.",
